      <!-- Section 2: Stochastic Resonance & ADHD -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-zinc-950 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          2. Resonansi Stokastik: Mengapa Brown Noise Menenangkan Otak ADHD
        </h2>
        <p>
          Gangguan Pemusatan Perhatian/Hiperaktivitas (ADHD) secara neurokimia ditandai transmisi dopamin disregulasi di korteks prefrontal dan jalur striatal. Menurut <strong>model Moderate Brain Arousal (MBA)</strong> yang diformulasikan neurosains Sikström dan Söderlund (2007), individu dengan dopamin basal rendah menderita defisiensi "sinyal-terhadap-derau" saraf internal, menyebabkan kegelisahan dan kegagalan fungsi eksekutif.
        </p>
        <p>
          Saat terpapar noise akustik frekuensi rendah kontinu (khususnya Brown noise), otak mengalami <strong>Resonansi Stokastik (SR)</strong>. Stochastic resonance is a non-linear biophysical phenomenon where optimal levels of background white/brown noise amplify sub-threshold neuronal signals, pushing them over the activation potential threshold without introducing cognitive distraction.
        </p>
        <p>
          In clinical trials, ADHD participants exposed to calibrated Brown and Pink noise demonstrated statistically significant improvements in working memory recall, reading comprehension, and task persistence compared to silent control conditions. The deep acoustic blanket occupies peripheral sensory channels, preventing the hyperactive thalamus from triggering involuntary attention shifts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Tinnitus Relief & Acoustic Masking -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-zinc-950 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          3. Manajemen Tinnitus: Masking Akustik & Inhibisi Residual
        </h2>
        <p>
          Subjective tinnitus is frequently a symptom of cochlear hair cell damage or auditory deafferentation. When the brainstem ceases to receive normal baseline frequency inputs from the inner ear, the primary auditory cortex (A1) increases its central gain, generating phantom auditory percepts (ringing, buzzing, or hissing).
        </p>
        <p>
          Lanskap suara akustik prosedural memberi manfaat klinis ganda bagi penderita tinnitus:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
          <li>
            <strong>Masking Akustik Lengkap:</strong> Noise Pink dan Brown spektrum lebar menaikkan ambang akustik ambien di atas level kenyaringan frekuensi tinnitus fantom, memberi kelegaan psikologis segera.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Inhibisi Residual & Habituasi:</strong> Extended exposure to continuous non-repetitive noise reduces the central gain hyperactivity of the auditory cortex. After turning the noise off, patients often experience minutes of temporary reduction or complete absence of the phantom ringing.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: Binaural Beats & Brainwave Entrainment -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-zinc-950 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          4. Neurosains Binaural Beats & Frequency Following Response (FFR)
        </h2>
        <p>
          Pertama ditemukan fisikawan Heinrich Wilhelm Dove pada 1839, <strong>binaural beats</strong> adalah ilusi auditori yang diproduksi di <em>Kompleks Olivari Superior</em>. When two pure sine wave tones with a slight frequency offset ($\Delta f$) are presented independently to each ear via stereo headphones, the brain integrates the phase differences and entrains electrical oscillations to match the difference frequency.
        </p>

